module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.WordTraps

/-!
# Traps for 74 blocks of periods 13 and 14, the closed sets that driven right halves settle into

Driven by a block of period 13 or 14 for 12,000 steps, a right half often ends inside a closed set of windows of 16
cells on which column 1 is fixed at the white phases: the closure of its window under both values of the cell beyond.
The natural scan with windows of 16 cells finds one for 52 blocks of period 13 and 56 of period 14 that the kit and the
finite game do not exclude and that the walls of [ThirteenTraps](ThirteenTraps.md) and
[FourteenTraps](FourteenTraps.md) do not carry. Here the kernel checks those of at most 3,000 states, for
34 blocks of period 13 and 40 of period 14.

* `nat<block>`, `nat<block>_check`: the traps, each passing the check of [WordTraps](WordTraps.md).
* `naturalTrapsLong`, `naturalTrapsLong_check`, `naturalTrapsLong_blocks`: the list, its check and its blocks.
* `naturalLong_absorption_excludes`: for each of them, if every finitely supported right half driven by the block
  enters its trap, the center column does not eventually repeat the block.

The tables come from `python -m computations.lock_chain --lean-long`. The natural-language argument is
`NaturalTrapsLong.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata

